From 3b0a6a5bee51d827a5463dde8426229cba90e905 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 04:19:47 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] port: Windows IOCP async expert-bundle reads (M2b)

Convert the Windows fallback in the moe_sparse_pipeline IO path from blocking
ReadFile+OVERLAPPED positioned reads to bounded IOCP async reads. The handle
opts into FILE_FLAG_OVERLAPPED and binds to a completion port; enqueue_read
claims a slot in a queue_depth-sized RequestData ring and issues a non-blocking
read; submit_and_wait harvests completions via GetQueuedCompletionStatusEx
(blocks for wait_nr, then drains ready ones without blocking); reap validates
the byte count, releases the ring slot, then fires the callback. No synthetic
completion is created for synchronous ReadFile success, so every request yields
exactly one completion.

The io_worker loop gains a Windows branch that fills the bounded ring before
waiting, so storage latency overlaps the token path, and drains all accepted
I/O on shutdown before the port and handle close.

Linux io_uring is byte-for-byte unchanged inside its existing preprocessor
branch (expert_cache.cpp is +54/-0; the Linux worker loop is untouched).

Speed effect is UNMEASURED - the streamed-21b verify run is RAM-gated on this
box and was not run. Do not quote a win until it is measured.

Ported-mechanism: io_uring bounded submit/reap semantics -> Win32 IOCP
Source-path: powerinfer/moe_sparse_pipeline/{iou.cpp,iou.hpp,expert_cache.cpp}
Evidence: research/local-inference/trial-evidence/110/PHASE2-ternary-rocmfpx-iocp.md
Origin: ArifiLabs/iocp-async
---
